1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,258
Face suddenly burning up mid-meeting, then drenched in sweat minutes later?

2
00:00:03,578 --> 00:00:08,182
Lower estrogen makes your body overreact to heat - coffee, wine, spicy food make it worse.

3
00:00:08,582 --> 00:00:15,514
Coffee can worsen hot flashes and night sweats - a Mayo Clinic study of 1,800+ women found this link.

4
00:00:15,834 --> 00:00:18,254
Try decaf, or skip it after noon.

5
00:00:18,654 --> 00:00:23,182
Wine and other alcohol widen blood vessels fast, causing a flush while you drink.

6
00:00:23,502 --> 00:00:26,425
Avoid it a few hours before bed, or pace it with water.

7
00:00:26,825 --> 00:00:31,750
Spicy food like hot wings triggers the same heat-sensing nerves as a hot flash, so sweat and flushing often follow.

8
00:00:32,070 --> 00:00:34,461
Sipping ice water through the meal can help take the edge off.

9
00:00:34,861 --> 00:00:38,979
None of this means giving these up for good - small tweaks in amount and timing help.

10
00:00:39,299 --> 00:00:45,913
More soy, like edamame or tofu, may help too - one review found it cut hot flash frequency over 20%.
